      "The 1.89% drop in Apple's stock on Monday was one of its worst post-keynote performances going back about a decade.",
      "Looking back to 2016, there was only one time that Apple shares logged a worse performance on the day of the WWDC keynote. That was in 2024, when shares fell 1.91%, according to Dow Jones Market Data.",
      "The median performance over that span was a 0.87% decline. But looking three months out, shares have tended to perform much better, with a median performance of a 15.1% gain."
